From f9135175ed10c6b7b26476d457b4ff6661fb22be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Duncan McQueen <dwmcqueen@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:17:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add support for Haiku on x86_64

Add Haiku (x86_64-*-haiku*) as a host:

- configure.ac: the host case, and the Makefiles for src/os/haiku.
  Haiku has dlopen() in libroot, so libdl is not needed.
- src/os/haiku/os.c: get the stack base and the number of CPUs from
  the Haiku kernel kit (get_thread_info() and get_system_info()).
  nativePhysicalMemory() returns 0, so JamVM uses the fixed default
  heap sizes: on Haiku, the mmap() of the maximum heap reserves the
  full size against RAM and swap. Haiku uses LIBRARY_PATH for native
  libraries.
- src/os/haiku/x86_64: the same files as src/os/bsd/x86_64. Haiku uses
  the System V AMD64 calling convention.
- src/class.c: the scandir() filter on Haiku takes a const argument.

Tested on Haiku R1/beta6 x86_64 with GNU Classpath (ingelabs master)
and the Haiku AWT peer: the default interpreter (inlining, direct,
threaded), threads, the garbage collector, AWT and Swing programs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
